Ports that the administrator opens to the LAN.

nftables reads every *.nft file in this directory into the input chain of
the sibyl table (/etc/nftables/sibyl.nft). A file holds rules only, with no
table or chain around them. For example, /etc/nftables/sibyl.d/whisper.nft:

    # Whisper, published by Arcane on host port 9000
    tcp dport 9000 accept

To limit a port to the LAN subnet:

    ip saddr 192.168.1.0/24 tcp dport 9000 accept

Check the rules, then load them:

    sudo nft -c -f /etc/sysconfig/nftables.conf
    sudo systemctl reload nftables

Rootless Podman publishes host ports of 1024 and higher only.
